skill: "deidentification-benchmark"
sections[3]:
  - "# deidentification-benchmark\n\nBenchmark a dataset's deidentification before it leaves its trust boundary: identifier classification, k-anonymity style measures, re-identification risk tests and differential privacy parameter checks against policy caps. Use before any analytics export, model training share or third-party data release.\n\nOwner: role-privacy-engineer (pod-gna, data_ai). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"dataset schema and sample; identifier taxonomy identifier-taxonomy.toon (direct, quasi); policy caps deid-policy.toon (minimum k, epsilon cap); release purpose statement\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/privacy/deidentification-report.toon with field classification, measures (k per quasi-identifier set), risk tests, dp parameters, verdict anonymized|pseudonymized\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Classify every field against identifier-taxonomy.toon: direct identifiers, quasi-identifiers (combination-capable), sensitive attributes; unclassified fields block the run.\n2. State the release purpose and the recipient class; the same dataset can pass for internal analytics and fail for an external share, and the verdict is per purpose.\n3. Measure k-anonymity for each planned quasi-identifier combination with run_command; the generalization steps applied are recorded, and k below the policy cap fails.\n4. Run the re-identification risk test: attempt re-identification against the plausible external sources named in policy; report the matched rate as the risk number, not a narrative.\n5. For noise-based releases, verify the differential privacy parameters against the epsilon cap and record delta, sensitivity assumptions and the mechanism used.\n6. Issue the verdict: anonymized only when re-identification risk is under the policy threshold with margin; otherwise pseudonymized, which keeps it in scope of privacy obligations and contract terms.\n7. List residual risks explicitly (small cells, rare values, linkage keys); a report without residual risks is incomplete and is returned.\n8. Write deidentification-report.toon; emit ask_question to the DPO-equivalent role for verdicts on external releases, and gate the export until the verdict is recorded.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nverdict gates the export; external releases countersigned by privacy owner.\n"
